{"schemaVersion":1,"systemCode":"BSI:srp-Cyrl:Latn:1958","dependencies":[],"metadata":{"authority_id":"bsi","id":"1958","language":"iso-639-2:srp","source_script":"Cyrl","destination_script":"Latn","name":"BS 2979:1958 Transliteration of Cyrillic and Greek characters - Table A, Serbian column (the British system)","url":"https://www.bsigroup.com","creation_date":"1958","confirmation_date":"2000-05","description":"BS 2979:1958, Table A, Serbian column: the \"British\" system for (modern) Cyrillic.\n    Table A is a five-column family table (East Slavonic: Russian, Ukrainian,\n    Byelorussian; South Slavonic: Bulgarian, Serbian and Macedonian).\n    This map is the Serbian rows of the column; the Macedonian-specific letters\n    (ѓ, ѕ, ќ) are a separate map.","notes":["NOTE 1 of Section 1: for extreme simplicity, when avoidance of ambiguity in back transliteration is not a paramount consideration, all accents, diacritics, etc., may be omitted in the English rendering; the document's own examples apply this (the document's own examples apply it). This map applies the table as printed, with the diacritics.","NOTE 2 of Section 1: Cyrillic characters for which the transliteration is given in parentheses, though no longer in official use, are sometimes found in the literature of the relevant language; this map renders them as given in the parentheses.","Rows 45 to 47 of Table A (the little yus, fita, izhitsa) are not rendered: their parenthesized cells are not legible beyond doubt in the scan and this map does not guess them. Table B (back transliteration) is out of scope; Table C is ISO/R9 and is cited against the existing iso corpus maps.","Row 38/40 choices: this map renders the hard sign with the right double quotation mark (U+201D) and the soft sign with the right single quotation mark (U+2019), the first option of each cell. The Serbian alphabet has no hard or soft sign.","The Serbian and Macedonian column gives the latinica, the existing Latin alphabet of Serbo-Croat, to avoid the confusion of an English transliteration. The footnote to Table A: in latinica, dj and gj are still sometimes found as alternatives to d with caron, but the practice is disappearing."]},"stages":[{"kind":"stage","name":"main","rules":[{"kind":"parallel","rules":[{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"А"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"A"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Б"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"B"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"В"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"V"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Г"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"G"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Д"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"D"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Ђ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Đ"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Е"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"E"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Ж"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Ž"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"З"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Z"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"И"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"I"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Ј"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"J"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"К"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"K"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Л"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"L"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Љ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Lj"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"М"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"M"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Н"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"N"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Њ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Nj"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"О"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"O"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"П"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"P"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Р"},"to":{"kind":"s